The Development plan:


(1) Process Model
The Tri-mic 
  A microphone that can record and do direction finding in 3D dimensions. 
allowing for data review and  analyses during and after capture.
The overall use of this device would be for pinpointing problems using sound or later export for audio analysis

(2)Requirements: Stakeholder & Engineering. (What Must it do)
It can accurately process and visually display sound waves in an easy to understand and measurable way.
Accurately point to the correctly identified direction.
Something although not required but nice to have would be the technology is durable and easy to work with. If it was dropped or exposed to little moisture
 It can continue to function as needed.

(3)Testing Plan. (How will I Demonstrate that it works?)
Place Tri-mic in a room and see if it can accurately pinpoint a single conversation around others in the same room.
It’s able to focus on one voice and mute other noise or impertinent voices.
It can distinguish direction from claps.

(4)Design Plan.(The how’s)
Research industry standard components 
Research Wave computation (MUSIC Algorithm)
Design CAD, PCB and materials, 
Purchase and design test material for variable mic distances and effectivity with using alternate sound calculation pipelines,
Once decided on a working solution build with improvements in mind  
purchase then test. 

(5)Design Reviews
- Approve design with engineers 
- Run cost estimations 
- Do market research
